# Defaults for `docker compose`. Any value here can be overridden in .env.local (later env files win).
#
# One proxy hop (Caddy, or Nginx on the host) sets X-Forwarded-For, which the per-client LLM limit uses.
# This is safe because port 3000 is bound to 127.0.0.1 by default, so only that proxy can reach the app.
# If you expose the app directly (APP_BIND=0.0.0.0, no proxy), put TRUST_PROXY=0 in .env.local —
# otherwise callers could spoof the header to get a fresh hourly quota.
TRUST_PROXY=1
